{title: Here We Come A-Wassailing}

{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

[E]Here we come a-wassailing,
among the leaves so green,
[A]Here we come a [E]wand'ring,
so [B]fair to be seen.

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus label="Chorus"}

Love and [E]joy come to [B]you,
And to [E]you your wassail [B]too,
And God [E]bless you and [A]send you a [C#m]happy new [E]year,
And God [B]send you a [A]happy new [E]year.

{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

[E]We are not daily be-eggars,
that beg from door to door,
[A]But we are neigh-bor’s [E]children,
whom [B]you have seen before.

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{column_break}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}

[E]Good master and good mistress,
As you sit beside the fire,
[A]Pray think of us poor [E]children,
Who [B]wander in the mire.

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}

[E]Call up the butler of the house,
put on his golden ring,
[A]Let him bring us all a [E]glass of beer,
and [B]better we shall sing.

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Repeat Chorus}
